body:
@cloppy could you help me out a bit with this as I don't have such a setup at hand?

From the documentation Microsoft [provides here](http://support.microsoft.com/kb/323308) `This issue occurs if the server sends a "Cache-control:no-store" header or sends a "Cache-control:no-cache" header.` , [this line](https://github.com/symfony/symfony/commit/1ab492394c#L0R248) should be changed but then it would render it incompatible with the rest of the browsers.

Maybe a detection of the user-agent is needed indeed?

@cloppy does the same thing applies to you?

Can you guys please test in other browsers as well? I can only test in Opera/Chrome/Firefox all Linux versions.
@romainneutron not a header expert here as well but I always like when IE puts one standard behind it :)

Thanks.

Not really. It really just seems to be the `Cache-Control` header.
So I cleaned it up a little bit and did the following

```
// Check if we need to remove Cache-Control for ssl encrypted downloads (IE <9 fix)
if(stristr($headers->get('Content-Disposition'), 'attachment')) {
    $this->headers->remove('Cache-Control');
}
```

Testes in IE8 & 9, Firefox 18.0.2 and Chrome 24
